The Node.js Xiaomi account, cryptographic, CS2 and MISS implementation is
adapted from the user's Xiaomi Camera Native for Home Assistant 0.3.0 archive.
That integration adapts Xiaomi protocol code from AlexxIT/go2rtc,
Copyright (c) 2022 Alexey Khit, under the MIT License reproduced in LICENSE.

Original go2rtc protocol reference revision documented in the supplied archive:
c245815e75e2a5fd60b4290f12bfc04e55a984d3
https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc/commit/c245815e75e2a5fd60b4290f12bfc04e55a984d3

Relevant upstream references:
- internal/xiaomi/xiaomi.go: device discovery and MISS session provisioning
- pkg/xiaomi/cloud.go: account authentication and signed cloud requests
- pkg/xiaomi/crypto/crypto.go: NaCl session derivation and ChaCha20 framing
- pkg/xiaomi/miss/client.go: authentication, video commands and frame formats
- pkg/xiaomi/miss/cs2/conn.go: LAN negotiation, TCP framing and UDP ordering/ACKs
- pkg/xiaomi/miss/producer.go: codec identifiers and timestamps
- https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc/pull/2531: MISS 0x112 movement operations

The source-only test/fixtures/reference_protocol files and emulator.py retain
the supplied Python implementation as an independent interoperability peer.
They are excluded from the installable npm package. Python is not required at
runtime. The native Node.js muxer, Homebridge integration, media lifecycle,
custom UI, FFmpeg SRTP delegate and tests are provided with this project.

Published crypto reference vectors used in automated tests:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7748
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8439
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6229
https://nacl.cr.yp.to/box.html

The Homebridge CameraController / CameraStreamingDelegate APIs and custom UI
API are provided by their respective Homebridge projects. The optional FFmpeg
dependency is a separate project and retains its own distribution notices.
No closed-source Xiaomi SDK, go2rtc executable or Home Assistant runtime is
included. Xiaomi, HomeKit, Apple and Homebridge names identify compatibility.
